     1	"""Runs the Q-path policy and applies its shared-weight updates.
     2	
     3	The per-environment Q state (dsyn, traces, ...) stays stacked on the device
     4	and is not split into per-environment lists like the rest of the policy
     5	carry. The jitted policy returns the new W_g (with the dsyn of every finished
     6	episode transferred in) and W_o (with the summed online updates); this wrapper
     7	writes them into the train params, the policy params and a pending policy
     8	sync. Separate copies are stored because the jax agent deletes old policy
     9	buffers when it swaps in a sync.
    10	"""
